// Naive schedule for example 08-histogram.
//
// Single worker `host`, every kernel placed there. The language-
// sanity slice of TASK-0044.04 (AC#1 + AC#2): smoke test that the
// algorithm parses, lowers, and emits bit-identical bytes on
// pthreads-sync AND mp-tcp-bufsync.
//
// No `transfer` directives: with everything on one worker no data
// crosses worker boundaries. PRD §6.3.4 only requires `transfer`
// for cross-worker edges. The link pass enforces that.
//
// No loop transforms: no `block=`, no `vectorize=`, no `partition=`.
// The point of the smoke test is "the algorithm runs sequentially
// and produces the reference"; the distributed schedule (see
// schedules/distributed.sched.nuc) is where the partition-axis
// schedule actually flexes — and is shipped as a stretch because
// the cross-worker partial-histogram combine is a substantively
// new ACFG/codegen shape vs the scalar-combine of 03-reduction.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host };

    place load_input  on host;
    place save_output on host;
    place bin_inc     on host;

    // No loop transforms.
    // No transfer directives — no cross-worker edges.
}
